# infra/prod/Caddyfile
#
# Automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt) for the API's own subdomain — needs a real
# DNS A record for this host pointed at the VM's public IP before Caddy can
# complete the ACME challenge (see infra/README.md).
#
# One hostname, two roots. A hostname is a box and a root is a service, and the
# two do not have to match: the Worker sends `/geo/*` and `/api/*` here with the
# path unchanged, and each goes to the container that answers it. Matching on a
# prefix and never on a route is what keeps adding a route a change to one
# server.

api.plei.me {
	handle /geo/* {
		reverse_proxy api:3000
	}
	handle /api/* {
		reverse_proxy app:3000
	}
	handle {
		respond "not found" 404
	}
}
